\subsection{Definitions and mathematical statement}
\paragraph{Statement recorded in the supplied source.}
Fix any odd positive N. For each k take the Z-algebra generated by prime-to-2N Hecke operators $T_l$ and l $S_l$ on the sum of all weight-i level-Gamma1(N) modular forms, including Eisenstein forms, for $1<=i<=k$; here $S_l$ acts in weight i by $l^{i-2}$ times the diamond operator. Complete each algebra by tensoring with Z2 and take their inverse limit under restriction. Must every irreducible component of its spectrum have Krull dimension exactly four?

\subsection{Short English statement}
