\section*{Dimension of the full two-adic Hecke algebra at odd level}

\subsection{OpenAI's claim}
OpenAI presents the following claims relevant to this question, with manuscript numbers following paper order in Sources. In manuscript 1 (family 010; 2026-10-05), the asserted result is that at any odd $\Gamma_1$ level, all irreducible components of the full two-adic Hecke algebra have Krull dimension four.

\subsection{Mathematical statement of the claimed result}
\paragraph{Manuscript 1.}
Fix any odd integer $N\ge1$. Let $M_i(N)$ be all complex modular forms of weight $i$ and level $\Gamma_1(N)$, including Eisenstein series. On their direct sum for $1\le i\le k$, let $T_{\le k}^{(2)}(N)$ be the $\mathbb Z$-algebra generated by $T_{\ell}$ and $\ell S_{\ell}$ at primes $\ell\nmid2N$, where $S_{\ell}$ acts as $\ell^{i-2}\langle\ell\rangle$. Form
\[
 T_2(N)=\varprojlim_k(\mathbb Z_2\otimes_{\mathbb Z}T_{\le k}^{(2)}(N)).
\]
The claimed conclusion is that every irreducible component of $\operatorname{Spec}T_2(N)$ has Krull dimension exactly four. All residual components are included; there is no cuspidality, slope or residual-irreducibility restriction.

\subsection{Outline of the argument}
For manuscript 1 (family 010; 2026-10-05), integral determinant laws and finite classical stages establish a Noetherian algebra. Cuspidal points on each component give lower bounds, while adjoint Galois cohomology and local quotients bound the tangent dimension from above.

